{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794667091,"nonce":"Sr04gGWng+IAVLSGp9PnIcOLSx8=","message":"Part of the cost is gone: consecutive faded siblings that paint plain primitives now share one offscreen atlas and one composite pass (d20f077), so a grid of them no longer costs a few render passes per card. A single group, or one of more than 512 px a side, a group cut by the viewport, or one that holds an image, a path, a mesh or a clip frame still takes the group-at-a-time path. The group is still painted every frame; a texture painted once and faded by a row is still the open option.","files":null}]}